Z||000000||doughboySE||01-20-2000||09:18 PM||||wow great this is working now <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>ok guys here is my question.<BR>i have a pioneer cd player (high output)<BR>i have a pioneer 100w mono amp<BR>i have a 80w sony amp<BR>i have 120w 4 by 10 in dash <BR>i have 80w 4 by 6 in the back.<BR>now the question , i want to install a sub and run it off of the 100w mono amp the way i had it in my VW GTI<BR>i have not got a sub yet nor a box has anyone installed one? where? and how? any help would be great thanx <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>p.s. how can i post a pic of my baby <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||01-21-2000||12:15 AM||||Some option that I have run across in my search for Bass: 8" in enclosures behind the passenger seat (subtract about 6" legroom), replacement console from RSM in Canada that uses 8" woofer (not included) about $200 US. I used to have REALLY cool Sony powered subwoofer tube mounted in front of my passenger seat (legs go over) with built in x-over,gain and reverb controls, but it is out of production and I can testify that it is theif bait.  My current plan is to mount Aura Bass Shakers inside my seatbacks augmented with 4" bazooka tubes mounted on rear window ledge. I have also seen a Jensen 8" tube woofer that you could mount in front of the passenger seat ad run off that amp, readily available at your local WalMart.  I would recommend either velcro mount or some good window tint and an alarm if you go that route.<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 01-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||01-21-2000||01:11 PM||||Doughboy,<P>This is a question almost as old as the Fiero itself!  There is not one answer.  I have seen many ways.  The best is shown on this link: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/banner.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/banner.htm</A>   These are installed behind the seats, but you lose no seat travel.  The rear window ledge is a false baffel.  Although some state that this was done with a purpose and some fuel vapors escape into that cavity, it has yet to been proven. Furthermore, I know personally of at least 20 of these sub installations and none have had any problems.<P>I went with a slightly different route.  My reasoning was that I seldomly have a passenger and when I do, 90% of the time it is my fiancee that does not require much leg room.  As you can guess, my sub is located in the passenger foot well.  I have also placed 6.5" mids in kick pods resting on the dead pedals.  A 12" sub will even fit in the footwell, but it will be tight.  Presently, my enclosure is constructed of MDF, but will probably be converted to Fiberglass/MDF to maximize internal volume and passenger foot space.  Also full MDF construction is not required since the car provides support on 5 sides of the box.  <P>Also some others have removed the spare tire and converted their front space into a sub box and ported it into the passneger compartment using ducting.  This is not terribly favorable since I have heard some complaints of the sound that the bass picks up while in the ducting.  <P>Then of course there are many other alternatives.  <P>Willilam T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||01-21-2000||01:45 PM||||The URL above should be:<P> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/</A> <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000004||batboy||01-21-2000||02:37 PM||||I used an 8" Rockford-Fosgate Punch sub in a small box and mounted it behind the passenger seat. I only lost 2-3 inches of seat travel. I mounted the amp behind the driver's seat. Everything is out of view to prying eyes and sounds pretty good too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||01-21-2000||02:51 PM||||sound,<P>Thanks for correcting my/your URL.  I hope you don't mind my referencing your system  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000006||1FST2M6||01-21-2000||03:44 PM||||In order to run all those speakers and looking at what you have you would have to run then all in series in order not to smoke your amp? I you want them to all run off that on amp. I have I won't go into detail but 2 sets of 4" midbass drivers and a set of tweaters in the factory (4x10)hole with one 10 Kicker Solobaric in the floor of the passenger (foot-well)(18mm Birchplywood and fiber-glas) You don't need lots of speakers to make a LOT of noise in your fiero.  Your going to have to cut the gain on whatever you use for the rear of the car to almost nothing. Due to the placement of the speakers. You'll hear them before you hear the front ones. You might want to leave them out all together. I have no idea how you could run all those speakers off one amp. Hoping that I'm misunderstanding you, All you'll need is a decent Highpass crossover at about 80Hz for the front (available throught <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com)" TARGET=_blank>www.crutchfield.com)</A>  and to run your sub from 80Hz down.  I'll try to post a pic or two of set up in a few minutes. You'll also probly want to replace your battery. I have an optima but Napa makes a better battery called an Orbital. and its like $30 cheaper than an optima... wish i'd know that before i bought mine! more to follow soon.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spyder||01-21-2000||03:57 PM||||“”Using what you got“”, this is what I would do:<BR>Use your CD player to run your 4x6s<BR>Use the 80 watt amp on your 4x10s<BR>Use the mono 100 watt on a new 8” sub behind the passenger seat.<BR>I built  custom boxes behind the seats once, long thin boxes that tapered at the top.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-21-2000||06:07 PM||||William--I guess it was a good thing that your '87 was broke when I saw you.  If it had been there I would have had to sit in it to hear the tunes.  I'm not sure if I would have fit.  Know what I mean, Verne?||||reg||1
Z||000009||spike||01-21-2000||06:33 PM||||I had 2 kenwood 10 inch subs in my Fiero GT and lost no seat travel at all. This summer I will install 2 12 inchers with no loss of seat travel. The subs are mounted in the cabin.||||reg||1
